1
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Wishes Can Come True.

2
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Annabelle's Wish is a family, animation, music film directed by Roy Wilson.

3
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Annabelle - a calf who has a special wish for Christmas - wants to be a reindeer
and help Santa Claus drive his sleigh as he delivers his presents!

4
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Annabelle's friends tell her not to get her hopes up, but to everyone's surprise, Santa does indeed meet up
with Annabelle, and the calf gets to help Santa make the holiday special for one young boy.

5
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Adult Billy / Narrator (voice), played by Randy Travis.

6
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Annabelle (voice), played by Kath Soucie.

7
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:18,000
Child Emily (voice), played by Aria Noelle Curzon.

8
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Grandpa Baker (voice), played by Jerry Van Dyke.

9
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Star (voice), played by Jennifer Darling.

10
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Slim (voice), played by Jerry Houser.

11
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Annabelle's Wish is a 1997 American direct-to-video animated Christmas film that revolves around a young calf who aspires to
fly like one of Santa Claus's reindeer, while forming a friendship with Billy, a young boy who cannot talk.

12
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Narrated by American country singer Randy Travis, it also stars voice actress Kath Soucie as the voice of
Annabelle and also features the voices of Jerry Van Dyke, Jim Varney and Clancy Brown.

13
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:54,000
Ralph Edwards Films released the film to video on October 21, 1997,
followed by a television broadcast later that year on Fox.

14
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
The film explores themes of holiday, reindeer, christmas.
